WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.450
Hi! Today we're going to add and subtract mixed numbers.

2
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:13.962
You use 2 and 1 third metres of red ribbon and 1 and a half metres of yellow ribbon to decorate the garden.

3
00:00:14.112 --> 00:00:19.986
How much is that altogether? First add the whole numbers: 2 plus 1 is 3.

4
00:00:20.136 --> 00:00:31.098
Then add the fractions. The denominators are different, so make them the same. 1 third is 2 sixths, 1 half is 3 sixths, and together they make 5 sixths.

5
00:00:31.248 --> 00:00:36.426
So altogether it is 3 and 5 sixths metres.

6
00:00:36.576 --> 00:00:42.114
Now subtraction: 3 and 1 quarter, minus 1 and 2 thirds.

7
00:00:42.264 --> 00:00:49.362
First make the denominators the same, 12: 3 and 3 twelfths minus 1 and 8 twelfths.

8
00:00:49.512 --> 00:00:58.890
3 twelfths is less than 8 twelfths, so we take 1 whole from the 3. One whole is 12 twelfths, so we get 2 and 15 twelfths.

9
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:10.818
Now we can subtract. 2 minus 1 is 1, and 15 twelfths minus 8 twelfths is 7 twelfths. The answer is 1 and 7 twelfths.

10
00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:15.282
One more: 1 and 3 quarters plus 2 and a half.

11
00:01:15.432 --> 00:01:23.322
Wholes: 1 plus 2 is 3. A half is 2 quarters, and 3 quarters plus 2 quarters is 5 quarters.

12
00:01:23.472 --> 00:01:29.994
5 quarters is 1 and 1 quarter, so the answer is 4 and 1 quarter.

13
00:01:30.144 --> 00:01:40.122
Watch out! Some pupils see that 3 is smaller than 8, so they do 8 minus 3 instead, and get 2 and 5 twelfths. That is wrong!

14
00:01:40.272 --> 00:01:47.298
We must rename 1 whole as 12 twelfths first. The correct answer is 1 and 7 twelfths.

15
00:01:47.448 --> 00:01:53.010
When the fraction part is too small, rename 1 whole first.

16
00:01:53.160 --> 00:02:02.562
Your turn! What is 4 and 1 sixth minus 2 and a half? Pause and think.

17
00:02:02.712 --> 00:02:17.466
A half is 3 sixths. Rename to get 3 and 7 sixths, minus 2 and 3 sixths, which is 1 and 4 sixths. In simplest form, that is 1 and 2 thirds. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:17.616 --> 00:02:27.258
Another one! What is 2 and 5 sixths plus 1 and 1 third? Pause and think.

19
00:02:27.408 --> 00:02:40.722
1 third is 2 sixths. The wholes make 3, and the fractions make 7 sixths, which is 1 and 1 sixth. Altogether that's 4 and 1 sixth. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:40.872 --> 00:02:50.226
Last one! What is 3 and a half minus 1 and 3 quarters? Pause and think.

21
00:02:50.376 --> 00:03:04.050
A half is 2 quarters. That is not enough, so take 1 whole from the 3 to get 2 and 6 quarters. Subtract 1 and 3 quarters to get 1 and 3 quarters. Did you get it right?

22
00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:14.826
Remember: make the denominators the same, then work out the wholes and the fractions separately. If the fraction part is too small to subtract, rename 1 whole.

23
00:03:14.976 --> 00:03:19.170
Now go and practise in your garden!

